       of the list just before it, and makes that setting's name clickable
       (BodyInlineJS.php). -->
  <dl class="vcm-form">
    <dt>Force a dismount when the array stops</dt>
    <dd><select id="s-force"><option value="yes">Yes</option><option value="no">No</option></select></dd>
  </dl>
  <blockquote class="inline_help">
    <p>Yes: a volume that is still in use when the array stops or the server shuts down is
       dismounted anyway, after its dependents were stopped. No: the array waits until the
       volume is free.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <dl class="vcm-form">
    <dt>Require HTTPS to mount</dt>
    <dd><select id="s-https"><option value="no">No</option><option value="yes">Yes</option></select>
        <p class="vcm-warning" id="s-https-warning" style="display:none">You are on plain HTTP right now.
          With this on, you cannot mount from this page until you open it over HTTPS.</p></dd>
  </dl>
  <blockquote class="inline_help">
    <p>Yes: a password is accepted only from a page opened over HTTPS; over plain HTTP the
       page offers no password field. Over plain HTTP the password would travel unencrypted
       over your network. Unlocking over SSH with <code>vcmount</code> always works.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <dl class="vcm-form">
    <dt>Show the volumes on the Main page</dt>
    <dd><select id="s-main"><option value="no">No</option><option value="yes">Yes</option></select></dd>
  </dl>
  <blockquote class="inline_help">
    <p>Yes: the Main page gets a section with the volumes, their locks to mount and dismount,
       and a link to open a mounted volume in the file manager.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <p id="vcs-error" class="vcm-error" hidden></p>
  <div class="vcm-buttons">
    <input type="button" id="vcs-apply" class="lock" value="Apply" disabled>
    <input type="button" id="vcs-done" class="lock" value="Done">
  </div>
</form>

